Both pipelines automate builds—but they are structured differently

In Jenkins, you can define pipelines in two styles: Declarative and Scripted.
They achieve the same goal, but differ in structure, flexibility, and readability.

Declarative Pipelines:
- Simpler and more structured
- Use pipeline { } syntax
- Best for most CI/CD use cases
- Easier to read, maintain, and enforce best practices

Scripted Pipelines:
- More flexible and powerful
- Use Groovy scripting
- Ideal for complex, conditional, or dynamic logic
- Require deeper Jenkins/Groovy knowledge

Declarative = cleaner, team-friendly syntax.
Scripted = advanced control and customization.
